# Temperance marker — cli#477 init banner collapse
- date: 2026-11-06
- branch: fix/init-banner-collapse
- scope-decision: Right thing — a cold adopter cannot read 201 lines, and the
  two facts they can act on are buried in it. Right way — move the inventory
  behind the flag that already means "show me the inventory" (--verbose, per
  cli#406), rather than add a second flag for the same job. Smallest shape —
  two files: src/commands/init.ts and its characterization test.
- blast radius: adopter-visible stdout only. The three machine surfaces are
  untouched and were each checked by hand: --json schema stayed 3,
  --dry-run output is byte-identical, .bassclef/init.manifest.json still
  records every file.
- brute-force check — considered deleting the per-file lines outright. Rejected:
  the debug read is real, and deleting would have weakened the characterization
  test instead of moving it.
- drift-trigger: if this starts touching the value-test block (cli#406) or the
  --dry-run path, stop and re-scope. Both are explicitly out of scope on #477.
